var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"python-deps/#Python-Dependencies-and-Rendering","page":"Python Dependencies","text":"GenLAProblems uses PythonCall to access the rendering stack and SymPy. The following packages are expected in the active Python environment:\n\nLAFigureSpecs\nmatrixlayout\njupyter_tikz\nsympy\n\nIf these are missing, rendering helpers like show_system, show_layout!, show_backsubstitution, show_solution, and show_ge_final will error. Make sure PythonCall points to a Python with the required packages (for example, set JULIA_PYTHONCALL_EXE).\n\nYou can explicitly initialize the Python stack with:\n\nGenLAProblems.ensure_pythoncall!()","title":"Python Dependencies and Rendering"},{"category":"section","location":"python-deps/#Smoke-render-helper","page":"Python Dependencies","text":"For a quick toolchain sanity check from Python:\n\npython render_smoke.py\n\nSet GENLAPROBLEMS_SMOKE_OUT to control the output directory.","title":"Smoke render helper"},{"category":"section","location":"python-deps/#Rendering-options-(render_opts)","page":"Python Dependencies","text":"High-level rendering helpers accept a render_opts keyword. This dictionary is passed through to the underlying renderers (LAFigureSpecs → matrixlayout → jupyter_tikz) and can include options such as:\n\ncrop\npadding (tuple order is (left, right, top, bottom) in SVG units; use mm_to_px to convert mm)\ntoolchain_name\nframe\nexact_bbox\n\noutput_dir is the canonical artifact directory (for TeX/PDF/SVG); tmp_dir is a legacy alias.","title":"Rendering options (render_opts)"},{"category":"section","location":"python-deps/#Troubleshooting","page":"Python Dependencies","text":"PythonCall can't find required packages\n\nEnsure PythonCall points to the Python where packages are installed: ENV[\"JULIA_PYTHONCALL_EXE\"] = \"/path/to/python\"\nInstall required packages in that Python: python -m pip install sympy (and install your local LAFigureSpecs, matrixlayout, jupyter_tikz packages)\n\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'LAFigureSpecs'\n\nVerify PYTHONPATH includes the local repos or install the packages into the Python env.\nIn tests, PYTHONPATH is set to include the local LA workspace repos such as LA/LAFigureSpecs and LA/matrixlayout.\n\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'matrixlayout'\n\nSame fix as above; ensure the module is on PYTHONPATH or installed.\n\nCould not import Python module sympy\n\nInstall sympy into the PythonCall interpreter or set JULIA_PYTHONCALL_EXE to a Python environment that already has sympy installed.\n\nPythonCall disabled or unavailable during precompile\n\nUnset GENLAPROBLEMS_DISABLE_PYTHONCALL or set JULIA_PYTHONCALL_EXE to a working Python.\nCall GenLAProblems.ensure_pythoncall!() from a runtime context (not precompile).","title":"Troubleshooting"},{"category":"section","location":"usage/#Usage-and-Quickstart","page":"Usage","text":"","title":"Usage and Quickstart"},{"category":"section","location":"usage/#Quickstart","page":"Usage","text":"using GenLAProblems\n\n# Build a small system and reduce to REF/RREF.\nA = [1 2 3; 2 4 6; 1 1 1]\nmatrices, pivots, desc = reduce_to_ref(A; gj=true)\n\n# Render a final GE table (requires Python stack).\nsvg = show_ge_final(matrices, desc, pivots; n_rhs=0)","title":"Quickstart"},{"category":"section","location":"usage/#Rendering-examples","page":"Usage","text":"using GenLAProblems\n\n# Example system\nA = [1 2; 3 4]\nb = [5, 6]\n\n# Render system as SVG\npb = ShowGE(A, b; output_dir=\"/tmp/la\")\nshow_system(pb; var_name=\"x\", fig_scale=1.2)\n\n# Access RHS block (or a single RHS column) from the final GE stack:\nrhs = rhs_block(pb)\nrhs1 = rhs_block(pb; b_col=1)\n\n# Render backsubstitution cascade\nU = [1 2; 0 3]\nshow_backsubstitution(U, b)\n\n# Render final GE table directly\nmatrices, pivots, desc = reduce_to_ref(A; gj=true)\nshow_ge_final(matrices, desc, pivots)\n\nRendering defaults to subdirectories under /tmp/la unless you pass output_dir or the compatibility alias tmp_dir.","title":"Rendering examples"},{"category":"section","location":"usage/#Inconsistent-systems","page":"Usage","text":"When a system is inconsistent, ShowGE records per-RHS status in pb.rhs_status (e.g., [:inconsistent, :consistent, ...]) and sets pb.status to :inconsistent or :mixed. In the rendered layout, inconsistent RHS columns are marked with a red × in the variable-summary row. The backsubstitution view is reduced to 0 = rhs with No Solution, and show_solution! returns an empty vector for those RHS columns. The solutions(pb) helper returns only consistent particular solutions.","title":"Inconsistent systems"},{"category":"section","location":"usage/#Pure-Julia-vs-Python-backed-APIs","page":"Usage","text":"Pure Julia (no Python needed):\n\nMatrix generation helpers (gen_*, unit_lower, lower, ref_matrix, rref_matrix)\nREF/RREF helpers (reduce_to_ref, normal_eq_reduce_to_ref, homogeneous_solutions)\nQR helpers (gram_schmidt_w, normalize_columns, gram_schmidt_stable, qr_layout)\nPolynomial helpers (charpoly)\n\nPython-backed (requires LAFigureSpecs, matrixlayout, jupyter_tikz, sympy via PythonCall):\n\nRendering helpers (show_layout!, show_system, show_backsubstitution, show_solution, show_ge_final)\nSymPy helpers (sym_*, sym_subs_numeric, sym_to_julia_*)","title":"Pure Julia vs Python-backed APIs"},{"category":"section","location":"usage/#Adjoint-inputs","page":"Usage","text":"Most top-level APIs accept AbstractMatrix and will work with adjoint wrappers like A'. In-place helpers that mutate matrices (e.g., row swap/eliminate utilities) require mutable matrices and will not work with Adjoint/Transpose inputs.","title":"Adjoint inputs"},{"category":"section","location":"#GenLAProblems","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for GenLAProblems.","title":"GenLAProblems"},{"category":"section","location":"#Compatibility-matrix","page":"Home","text":"Component Minimum Notes\nJulia 1.9 Tested with 1.9–1.10.\nPythonCall 0.9 Required for LAFigureSpecs/matrixlayout interop.\nLAFigureSpecs current Spec generation + algorithms.\nmatrixlayout current TeX + SVG rendering.\njupyter_tikz itikz_port TeX toolchains + SVG.\nTeX toolchain TeX Live 2022+ Needed for SVG rendering.","title":"Compatibility matrix"},{"category":"section","location":"#CLI-quick-checks","page":"Home","text":"Run a smoke render to validate toolchains:\n\npython render_smoke.py\n\nSet GENLAPROBLEMS_SMOKE_OUT to control the output directory.","title":"CLI quick checks"},{"category":"section","location":"#Guides","page":"Home","text":"Usage and quickstart\nPython dependencies and rendering\nExact arithmetic and SymPy helpers\n\n","title":"Guides"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.DoElimination","page":"Home","text":"DoElimination\n\nRecord an elimination operation applied to the matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.DoElimination"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.DoRowExchange","page":"Home","text":"DoRowExchange\n\nRecord a row exchange operation applied to the matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.DoRowExchange"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.DoScaling","page":"Home","text":"DoScaling\n\nRecord a scaling operation applied to the matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.DoScaling"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.Finished","page":"Home","text":"Finished\n\nMark the end of a reduction sequence.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.Finished"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.FoundPivot","page":"Home","text":"FoundPivot\n\nRecord a pivot discovery during elimination.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.FoundPivot"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.RequireElimination","page":"Home","text":"RequireElimination\n\nDescribe a required elimination step at a given pivot.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.RequireElimination"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.RequireRowExchange","page":"Home","text":"RequireRowExchange\n\nDescribe a required row exchange step during elimination.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.RequireRowExchange"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.RequireScaling","page":"Home","text":"RequireScaling\n\nDescribe a required scaling step when normalizing pivot rows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.RequireScaling"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenLAProblems.SVGOut","page":"Home","text":"SVGOut(svg::String)\n\nWrapper type for SVG output from show_ge_final, enabling rich display in IJulia.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.SVGOut"},{"category":"method","location":"#AbstractAlgebra.charpoly-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Complex{Int64}}}","page":"Home","text":"charpoly(A::AbstractMatrix{Complex{Int64}})\n\nCompute the characteristic polynomial for complex integer matrices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AbstractAlgebra.charpoly"},{"category":"method","location":"#AbstractAlgebra.charpoly-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Complex{Rational{Int64}}}}","page":"Home","text":"charpoly(A::AbstractMatrix{Complex{Rational{Int64}}})\n\nCompute the characteristic polynomial over the Gaussian rationals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AbstractAlgebra.charpoly"},{"category":"method","location":"#AbstractAlgebra.charpoly-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Int64}}","page":"Home","text":"charpoly(A::AbstractMatrix{Int64})\n\nCompute the characteristic polynomial over rationals for integer matrices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AbstractAlgebra.charpoly"},{"category":"method","location":"#AbstractAlgebra.charpoly-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Rational{Int64}}}","page":"Home","text":"charpoly(A::AbstractMatrix{Rational{Int64}})\n\nCompute the characteristic polynomial over rationals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AbstractAlgebra.charpoly"},{"category":"method","location":"#Base.show-Tuple{IO, MIME{Symbol(\"image/svg+xml\")}, GenLAProblems.SVGOut}","page":"Home","text":"show(io::IO, ::MIME\"image/svg+xml\", x::SVGOut)\n\nEmit the SVG payload for rich notebook display.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.show"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems._int_range-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"_int_range(maxint, has_zeros) -> AbstractVector{Int}\n\nReturn the integer range used to populate random matrices, optionally including zero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems._int_range"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems._is_missing_python_module-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"load_LAFigureSpecs() -> LAFigureSpecs\n\nLoad the Python LAFigureSpecs module via PythonCall.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems._is_missing_python_module"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems._keep_file_output_parts-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"show_layout!(pb; array_names=nothing, show_variables=true, fig_scale=1, output_dir=nothing, output_stem=nothing)\n\nRender the GE layout for a ShowGE problem as SVG. Use output_dir and output_stem to retain TeX/PDF/SVG artifacts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems._keep_file_output_parts"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems._system_matrix_rhs-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"show_system(pb; b_col=1, var_name=\"x\", fig_scale=1)\n\nRender the linear system associated with a ShowGE problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems._system_matrix_rhs"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.create_cascade!-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"create_cascade!(pb::ShowGE; b_col=1, var_name=\"x\")\n\nInitialize cascade state for substitution displays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.create_cascade!"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.decorate_ge-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"decorate_ge(description, pivot_cols, sizeA; kwargs...)\n\nCompute pivot markers, background highlights, and path traces for GE layouts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.decorate_ge"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.eig_matrices_from_spec-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"eig_matrices_from_spec(spec; orthonormal=true)\n\nBuild (Λ, V) from an eigen-table spec dictionary (as returned by LATeachingSuite.eig_bundle / LAFigureSpecs.eig_tbl_spec). Uses qvecs when available and orthonormal=true, otherwise uses evecs. The matrix type is preserved.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.eig_matrices_from_spec"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.eliminate-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"eliminate(A, pivot_row, row, alpha)\n\nAdd alpha * pivot_row to row in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.eliminate"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.ensure_pythoncall!-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"ensure_pythoncall!()\n\nExplicitly initialize PythonCall and return the module handle. Raises a clear error when PythonCall is disabled or unavailable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.ensure_pythoncall!"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.find_pivot-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"find_pivot(A, row, col) -> Int\n\nFind a nonzero pivot in column col at or below row; returns -1 if none found.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.find_pivot"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.ge_variable_type-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"ge_variable_type(pivot_cols, n) -> Vector{Bool}\n\nReturn a Boolean vector marking pivot columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.ge_variable_type"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gen_cx_eigenproblem-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"gen_cx_eigenproblem(evals_no_conj; maxint=1) -> S, Λ, S_inv, A\n\nGenerate a complex eigenproblem from non-conjugate eigenvalues.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gen_cx_eigenproblem"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gen_eigenproblem-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"gen_eigenproblem(e_vals; maxint=3) -> S, Λ, S_inv, A\n\nGenerate a random eigenproblem with prescribed eigenvalues.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gen_eigenproblem"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gen_rhs-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"gen_rhs(A, pivot_cols; maxint=3, num_rhs=1, has_zeros=false) -> X, B\n\nGenerate a random RHS matrix B = A*X consistent with given pivot columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gen_rhs"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gen_svd_problem-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"gen_svd_problem(m, n, σ; maxint=3) -> U, Σ, Vt, A\n\nGenerate an SVD problem with specified singular values. Returns orthogonal factors U, Vt, the diagonal matrix Σ, and the product A = U * Σ * Vt.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gen_svd_problem"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gen_symmetric_eigenproblem-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"gen_symmetric_eigenproblem(e_vals; maxint=5, with_zeros=false, general=true) -> Q, Λ, A\n\nGenerate a symmetric eigenproblem with prescribed eigenvalues.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gen_symmetric_eigenproblem"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gram_schmidt_stable-Union{Tuple{AbstractMatrix{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"gram_schmidt_stable(A::AbstractMatrix{T}; reorthogonalize=false) where T<:Number\n\nCompute a stable Gram-Schmidt QR factorization, optionally reorthogonalizing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gram_schmidt_stable"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.gram_schmidt_w-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"gram_schmidt_w(A) -> Matrix\n\nNaive Gram-Schmidt producing an integer matrix of orthogonalized columns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.gram_schmidt_w"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.homogeneous_solutions-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Compute the homogeneous solution from a system in Reduced Row Echelon Form\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.homogeneous_solutions"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.interchange-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"interchange(A, row_1, row_2)\n\nSwap rows row_1 and row_2 in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.interchange"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.is_none_val-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"is_none_val(x) -> Bool\n\nReturn true when x is :none or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.is_none_val"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.l_show_svd-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Home","text":"l_show_svd(A, U, Σ, Vt, rankA)\n\nDisplay an SVD factorization with block structure separating the rank and null space components.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.l_show_svd"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.la_version-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"la_version(), la_build(), ml_version(), ml_build()\n\nReturn version/build strings exposed by the Python packages LAFigureSpecs and matrixlayout. These require PythonCall at runtime.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.la_version"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.load_matrixlayout-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"load_matrixlayout() -> matrixlayout\n\nLoad the Python matrixlayout module via PythonCall.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.load_matrixlayout"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.lower-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"L = lower(m,n; maxint=3)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.lower"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.lower-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"L = lower(m; maxint=3)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.lower"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.mm_to_px-Tuple{Real}","page":"Home","text":"mm_to_px(mm) -> Float64\n\nConvert millimeters to px-equivalent SVG units (96 px per inch).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.mm_to_px"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.non_zero_entry-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"non_zero_entry(A, row, col, gj) -> Bool\n\nReturn true if there is a nonzero entry below (and above for GJ) in column col.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.non_zero_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.normal_eq_reduce_to_ref-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"normal_eq_reduce_to_ref(A; n=nothing, gj=false, find_pivot=find_pivot)\n\nReduce A (or its normal equations) to REF/RREF, returning matrices, pivots, and trace.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.normal_eq_reduce_to_ref"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.normalize_columns-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"normalize_columns(int_W) -> Matrix\n\nNormalize integer columns, introducing symbolic square roots when needed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.normalize_columns"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.particular_solution-Tuple{Any, AbstractVecOrMat, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Compute the particular solution from a system in Reduced Row Echelon Form\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.particular_solution"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.particular_solution-Tuple{Any, Int64, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Compute the particular solution from a system in Augmented Reduced Row Echelon Form\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.particular_solution"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.px_to_mm-Tuple{Real}","page":"Home","text":"px_to_mm(px) -> Float64\n\nConvert px-equivalent SVG units to millimeters (96 px per inch).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.px_to_mm"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.py_show_svg-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"py_show_svg(svg)\n\nDisplay an SVG in a Python notebook (e.g., %%julia cell) via IPython.display.SVG. Accepts SVGOut, raw SVG strings, or PythonCall.Py SVG objects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.py_show_svg"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.qr_layout-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"qr_layout(A) -> Any\n\nReturn a LaTeX-ready layout of the QR construction steps.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.qr_layout"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.qr_matrices_dict_from_grid-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"qr_matrices_dict_from_grid(mats)\n\nReturn QR matrices as a plain dict for JSON-friendly usage.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.qr_matrices_dict_from_grid"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.qr_matrices_from_grid-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"qr_matrices_from_grid(mats)\n\nExtract QR-related matrices from a Gram–Schmidt QR grid (as returned by LATeachingSuite.qr_figure). Returns (A, W, WtA, WtW, S, Qt, Q, R) as a named tuple. The matrix type is preserved (Julia or SymPy).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.qr_matrices_from_grid"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.ref!-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"ref!(pb; n_rhs=:None, gj=false, normal_eq=false)\n\nCompute REF/RREF data for a ShowGE problem and attach pivot metadata.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.ref!"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.rhs_block-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"rhs_block(pb::ShowGE; step=:final, b_col=nothing)\n\nReturn the RHS block from a GE stack. Use step to select a specific matrix stack index (1-based) or :final for the last step. If b_col is provided, returns a single RHS column vector; otherwise returns the full RHS block.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.rhs_block"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.show_backsubstitution!-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"show_backsubstitution!(pb; b_col=1, var_name=\"x\", fig_scale=1)\n\nRender the back-substitution cascade for a ShowGE problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.show_backsubstitution!"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.show_ge_final-Tuple","page":"Home","text":"show_ge_final(args...; kwargs...) -> SVGOut\n\nRender only the final GE table from matrices[end][end].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.show_ge_final"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.show_solution!-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"show_solution!(pb; b_col=1, var_name=\"x\", fig_scale=1)\n\nRender the solution vector/form for a ShowGE problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.show_solution!"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.show_solution-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"show_solution(matrices; var_name=\"x\", fig_scale=1, output_dir=nothing, tmp_dir=nothing, render_svg=true)\n\nRender the standard solution form from the final augmented matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.show_solution"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.show_svg-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"show_svg(svg)\n\nAlias for py_show_svg, for notebook-friendly SVG display.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.show_svg"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.solutions-Union{Tuple{ShowGE{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Number","page":"Home","text":"solutions(pb::ShowGE) -> xp, xh\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.solutions"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.split_R_RHS-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"Home","text":"split_R_RHS(R_RHS, num_rhs) -> (R, RHS)\n\nSplit an augmented matrix into the coefficient block and RHS block.\n\nIf num_rhs is a vector of group sizes, returns (R, rhs_groups) where rhs_groups is a vector of RHS block matrices in order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.split_R_RHS"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.svd_matrices_from_spec-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"svd_matrices_from_spec(spec; reduced=true)\n\nBuild (U, Σ, V, rank) from an SVD spec dictionary (as returned by LATeachingSuite.svd_bundle / LAFigureSpecs.svd_tbl_spec). The matrix type is preserved: if the spec contains SymPy objects, returns SymPy matrices; otherwise returns Julia matrices. When reduced=true, only nonzero singular value groups are included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.svd_matrices_from_spec"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.symbol_vector-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"symbol_vector(s, indices) -> Vector{Symbol}\n\nReturn a vector of Symbol names like s_i for the given indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.symbol_vector"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenLAProblems.symbols_matrix-Tuple{String, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"symbols_matrix(s, row_indices, col_indices)\n\nCreate a matrix of symbolic variables using syms with names like s_{i,j}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.symbols_matrix"},{"category":"section","location":"exact-arithmetic/#Exact-Arithmetic-and-SymPy-Helpers","page":"Exact Arithmetic","text":"","title":"Exact Arithmetic and SymPy Helpers"},{"category":"section","location":"exact-arithmetic/#Exact-QR-helpers","page":"Exact Arithmetic","text":"gram_schmidt_stable supports exact inputs (e.g., Rational, Complex{Rational}), but the exact path returns matrices with symbolic square roots (via Symbolics). This means results are Matrix{Any} and may contain Symbolics.sqrt(...) terms. If you need purely numeric results, use floating inputs or post-process the symbolic output.\n\ngram_schmidt_w produces exact, rational-valued orthogonalized columns for integer inputs and normalize_columns introduces symbolic square roots as needed. These helpers are intended for pedagogical output and may not be suitable for numeric downstream computations without additional conversion.","title":"Exact QR helpers"},{"category":"section","location":"exact-arithmetic/#Exact-vs-numeric-(quick-comparison)","page":"Exact Arithmetic","text":"Topic Exact inputs (Rational, Complex{Rational}) Numeric inputs (Float64, ComplexF64)\ngram_schmidt_stable Returns symbolic square roots; Matrix{Any} Returns numeric Q, R\ngram_schmidt_w Rational orthogonal columns Not intended for floats\nnormalize_columns Uses Symbolics.sqrt when needed Returns numeric Q\nDownstream math May need symbolic handling Direct numeric workflows","title":"Exact vs numeric (quick comparison)"},{"category":"section","location":"exact-arithmetic/#SymPy-helpers","page":"Exact Arithmetic","text":"sym_mat/sym_vec convert Julia arrays to SymPy matrices and preserve exact rationals (Rational) and complex rationals (Complex{Rational}) as SymPy rationals and I. If you pass mixed-type Matrix{Any} inputs, SymPy conversion can still be sensitive to PythonCall’s ndarray handling; prefer uniform numeric or symbolic arrays.\n\nsym_subs_numeric returns a Julia array only when all symbols are substituted; otherwise it returns a SymPy matrix. Use sym_to_julia_mat or sym_to_julia_vec to force conversion when appropriate.","title":"SymPy helpers"},{"category":"section","location":"exact-arithmetic/#Known-limitations","page":"Exact Arithmetic","text":"Mixed-type Matrix{Any} inputs can trigger PythonCall conversion issues in some environments.\nSome rendering helpers require the full Python stack; without it they will throw errors.\nSymbolic outputs from exact QR are not guaranteed to simplify unless you apply Symbolics/SymPy simplification.","title":"Known limitations"},{"category":"function","location":"exact-arithmetic/#GenLAProblems.SymPyHelpers.sym_subs_numeric","page":"Exact Arithmetic","text":"sym_subs_numeric(A, subs) -> Union{Py, AbstractArray}\n\nSubstitute subs into a SymPy matrix or Julia matrix convertible to SymPy. subs can be a Dict or list of pairs. Returns a SymPy matrix if symbols remain; otherwise returns a Julia numeric array.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenLAProblems.SymPyHelpers.sym_subs_numeric"}]
}
